    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    FULL VERSION HISTORY
    Public releases from v1.0.0 through the current v1.0.11 update.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.11  •  Current Update
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Promoted the completed v1.0.11 Alpha work into the public v1.0.11 update
      while preserving Build 132's confirmed readiness spacing and behavior.
    • Added two simple Enhanced advertising modes: USA / Europe by Time and
      All Regions by Time.
    • Advertise Region now follows each user's local PC time, with All Regions
      remaining the default schedule.
    • Added the two-line singleplayer Startup-ready HUD with the configured
      Start Session hotkey.
    • Protected live GTA Online characters, outfits, hair, and loaded Lua state
      by blocking automatic settings-profile loading after Online is active.
    • Locked hidden advertising limits to 30 / 25 players and Legacy counts to
      5 / 10, including automatic migration away from older custom values.
    • Added duplicate-instance protection for subscribed and local Startup
      copies so only one instance can register features.
    • Added manual read-only 30-method and 50-method Cherax host diagnostics.
    • Expanded Cherax Host Finder support across Standard, Premium, and Prime
      while preserving safe read-only host testing.
    • Strengthened Enhanced NAT and Advertise Region recovery, including native
      fallbacks and automatic NAT override reapplication after rescans.
    • Added 10-second departed-modder HUD cleanup with a stale-entry fallback.
    • Confirmed all 83 supplied Cherax flag labels as modder evidence in the
      HUD while keeping classification separate from automatic attack response.
    • Hid the unfinished Lobby Finder panel while preserving its backend for
      future development.
    • Reworked Kick Defense so a single generic KICK / VOTE_KICK protection
      reaction is treated as unverified evidence instead of a confirmed attack.
    • Split automatic crash and kick handling: crash removal remains ON by
      default, while experimental repeated-kick removal starts OFF.
    • Added duplicate-reaction filtering and multi-player reaction-storm
      suppression so rapid false detections cannot remove several players.
    • Unverified kick reactions no longer create Modders HUD entries, permanent
      RID attack records, or automatic Smart Kicks.
    • Added optional diagnostic logging and a strict two-reaction threshold for
      users who deliberately enable experimental kick auto-removal.
    • Rebuilt Startup's visible Cherax console output around a compact colored
      banner, version details, and short readiness summaries.
    • Removed routine NAT scan names, addresses, resolver hashes, schedule ticks,
      worker queues, session-selection chatter, and other boot diagnostics from
      the normal LE / EE console.
    • NAT and Enhanced Advertise Region internals remain available inside support
      diagnostics without overwhelming average users.
    • NAT Override and Enhanced Advertise Region messages now appear only when a
      value genuinely changes, using clear previous-to-new wording.
    • Prevented the queued HUD fallback from repeating Startup's completed boot
      NAT scan and producing a second duplicate scan sequence.
    • Expanded the clean console presentation into the complete Startup identity
      block with the full ASCII logo, tagline, developer, Discord, version, build,
      update date, separator, Happy Gaming message, and readiness summaries.
    • Preserved the spacious reference formatting while keeping normal LE / EE
      logs quiet and retaining color-coded banner, metadata, and success output.
    • Fixed the full console banner not appearing on some Cherax builds because
      the colored logger was being called with an empty sender name.
    • Moved the banner into its own early queued load step so it appears directly
      after Cherax reports that Startup.lua loaded successfully.
    • Kept the later initialization banner call as a duplicate-safe fallback and
      preserved dynamic NAT and Enhanced Advertise Region readiness summaries.
    • Consolidated the visible identity banner into one multiline console entry
      so its logo, separators, tagline, and metadata no longer repeat Cherax
      timestamps or [Startup] prefixes on every displayed line.
    • Replaced “Skip the Manual Labor” with the cleaner GTA-focused tagline
      “Startup - From Launch to Lobby.”
    • Kept normal status, warning, NAT-change, and region-change messages on the
      standard Startup logger path so useful events remain easy to identify.
    • Added Manually Pick a Region as a third Enhanced advertising mode alongside
      USA / Europe by Time and All Regions by Time.
    • Added a manual eight-region dropdown that appears only while manual mode is
      selected and keeps the chosen region fixed until another mode is selected.
    • Enforced one-at-a-time region modes so selecting any mode automatically
      disables the other two without leaving Enhanced scheduling in a mixed state.
    • Recolored Startup's terminal identity with its own violet, aqua, gold, blue,
      green, and white ANSI palette inspired by DriftGod's raw terminal banner.
    • Quieted the Startup tab preference save and Event Music pulse messages so
      normal users no longer see unnecessary console chatter.
    • Grouped the Enhanced Advertise Region readiness summary directly beneath
      the raw NAT pattern count without timestamps or a [Startup] prefix.
    • Standardized readiness spacing to exactly one blank line between NAT and
      region summaries, followed by a compact four-line break before normal
      Startup event messages such as a successful NAT Override change.
    • Known limitation: Enhanced advertising may fill more slowly than Legacy.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.10  •  Production Stability
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Fixed the notorious blank Cherax menu bug and removed unsafe discovery
      paths that could prevent Startup's interface from appearing.
    • Fixed theme-loading errors and Startup pressing ESC during load.
    • Fixed Enhanced Advertise Session and Advertise Region support.
    • Improved NAT HUD behavior, session startup, local storage, and general
      Legacy / Enhanced stability.
    • Fixed saved-settings discovery so every JSON profile under
      Cherax\Settings can be listed safely.
    • Added a read-only 30-method Cherax host diagnostic and optional host
      finder workflow without kicks, crashes, entities, or forced interaction.
    • Added the Prime 20+ initial-lobby filter with a stabilization wait.
    • Improved kick-defense confirmation to reduce false reactions from
      harmless leave-vehicle events.
    • Added the embedded 83-name modder-flag catalog and separated confidence,
      crash, kick, RAC, explosion, and ignored categories.
    • Expanded support diagnostics, local RID history, player-population
      guidance, and guided setup reliability.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.9  •  HUD, Defense & Onboarding
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Expanded the optional Session HUD with Session Host, Script Host, Next
      Host, friends, NAT, region, speaking players, and modder reasons.
    • Added configurable HUD ordering while keeping Connected Players fixed at
      the bottom.
    • Added automatic crash-attempt defense, safer kick confirmation, Country
      Filter controls, and persistent local RID records.
    • Added the guided first-run setup, What's New popup, Support ZIP workflow,
      and update simulations.
    • Improved Prime routing, NAT detection, conservative protection defaults,
      and Enhanced-only region controls.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.8  •  Confirmed Production Baseline
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Promoted the confirmed v1.0.7 Alpha foundation into a production release.
    • Preserved Startup automation, edition routing, matchmaking, HUD, defense,
      guide, config, and theme-safety behavior.
    • Excluded unfinished experimental support features from the public build.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.7 Alpha  •  Theme Safety
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Turned Auto-Load Theme and Random Theme On Startup OFF by default for
      safer startup behavior.
    • Added a one-time migration for existing users while preserving later
      manual theme choices.
    • Kept manual theme loading and selection fully available.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.6  •  Recovery & Polish
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Promoted the current feature set into a production release.
    • Added the compact Discover More Scripts dropdown.
    • Added Config Reset & Recovery tools for restoring Startup defaults safely.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.5  •  Full Startup Automation
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Delivered automatic session startup and smart advertising with
      edition-aware Standard, Premium, and Prime routing.
    • Combined saved-settings, theme, and selected-Lua automation with master
      and per-file delays.
    • Added GTA-native session notifications, optional Player & Mod UI,
      persistent modder / RAC tracking, and Battleye host defense.
    • Hardened UI asset loading and added simulation, testing, time, world,
      guide, and config tools.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.4  •  Persistent Modder Tracking
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Added persistent in-session modder tracking and readable detection reasons.
    • Added direct RAC report-flag detection with display-only RAC handling.
    • Added explicit roster cleanup when players leave, are blocked, or are
      kicked.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.3  •  Activity Feed & Guide
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Turned join, block, reason, and leave notices into an animated stacking
      session activity feed.
    • Added slide-in motion, smooth upward movement, fade-out, and a looping
      live demonstration.
    • Combined Tips and How To into one Guide area and moved script discovery
      into Credits.
    • Added the Main action that creates the required default Cherax settings
      profile.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.2  •  File & First-Run Reliability
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Fixed first-run initialization and unload saving by using Cherax FileMgr
      directory creation.
    • Removed the remaining shell-execution path.
    • Kept browser opening capability-based with a clipboard fallback.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.1  •  Welcome, Routing & Modder HUD
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Added the required one-time Startup welcome with Discord copy / browser
      actions and saved completion state.
    • Improved active Standard / Premium versus Prime session routing.
    • Added compatibility fallback for renamed or missing Advertise Count
      controls.
    • Added the live Modders HUD and the community script showcase.

    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    v1.0.0  •  First Public Release
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Released automatic default settings save / load and edition-aware public
      session routing.
    • Added selected Lua loading with master and per-file delays plus theme
      automation.
    • Added matchmaking tools, day / night controls, host-defense guidance, and
      the saved Pause / Break session hotkey.
    • Included compact guidance, script discovery, one-time community
      onboarding, and Credits.

